    {
      "type": "Note",
      "size": [
        1120,
        230
      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Open this workflow in a fresh tab. Press the editor Run triangle in “orbit brush” if it is not running. The top row is a model-free WebGPU chain: Math → Crop → Transform → Feedback → Blur → Corner Pin → Composite → Stage. Draw in the annotation node to add transparent ink. Local preview freeze/minimize does not pause downstream frames. Use texture Reset to clear feedback history. WebGPU is required for the live texture chain; queued operators use the Comfy backend."
      ],
      "id": 22,
      "pos": [
        0,
        -100
      ],
      "order": 21,
      "mode": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "title": "START HERE · Creative Stage Showcase"
    },
    {
      "type": "Note",
      "size": [
        1120,
        230
      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Select final stage, then D toggles the graph backdrop; Alt+W toggles its overlay; Alt+F fills the Comfy viewport and restores the previous rectangle. These same controls are available on the node. Overlay edges reveal opacity, pin, click-through and close. Alt+P hides the graph for presentation. Alt+Shift+Z hides Comfy chrome; Alt+Shift+I toggles graph diagnostics. Drawing Alt+W opens the active editor as an annotation overlay; Alt+Z reveals drawing tools. Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Backspace clears the drawing. Shortcuts do not intercept code typing."
      ],
      "id": 23,
      "pos": [
        1220,
        -100
      ],
      "order": 22,
      "mode": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "title": "OUTPUT & PRESENTATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "Note",
      "size": [
        1010,
        230
      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Tixy exposes editable code parameters. The GLSL image shader consumes the brush IMAGE and a regular Comfy Float wire. Markdown supports formula rendering. Camera flip, resolution and sampling controls are available after you choose a source; capture requires your explicit Start / Share action. The SDXS lane starts in Comfy Queue, so opening this demo does not start inference. It requires macOS 14+ on Apple silicon and installed Core ML models. Use the stage prompt as a starting point."
      ],
      "id": 24,
      "pos": [
        2440,
        -100
      ],
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "title": "EXPLORE THE OTHER LANES"
    },
    {
      "type": "Note",
      "size": [
        660,
        380
      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "The main stage needs no models. SDXS is deliberately in Comfy Queue; install models using scripts/setup_macos.sh then scripts/download_models.sh before queuing the whole graph. Choose an installed model_path and use the node Live dropdown + Play for realtime inference. One generator at a time is best while benchmarking. Camera/screen remain off until you start them. For other language demos, open ꘇ-Livecode-Languages or ꘇ-Livecode-Math alongside this workflow."
      ],
      "id": 25,
      "pos": [
        2790,
        2110
      ],
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "title": "OPTIONAL GENERATION · before queuing"
    }
